{
  "name": "Qualify Substack Newsletters for B2B Sponsorships & Extract Top Posts Engagement",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Qualify Substack Newsletters for B2B Sponsorships & Extract Top Posts Engagement\n\n**Actor:** [Substack Newsletter Leads, Authors & Posts Scraper: Engagement & Sponsorship Data](https://apify.com/storeintel/substack-newsletter-leads-posts-scraper)\n\n### Production Multi-Branch Architecture (11 Nodes)\n1. **Dual Triggers:** Daily 08:00 schedule or 1-click manual test.\n2. **Apify Extraction:** Runs browserless HTTP scraper `substack-newsletter-leads-posts-scraper`.\n3. **Clean & Deduplicate:** Filters invalid items and removes duplicate leads.\n4. **Custom JS Lead Scoring:** Assigns `lead_score` (0–100) + `priority_tier` using domain signals.\n5. **Conditional Routing (`IF >= 70`):**\n   - **Tier 1 (High Intent):** Generates AI personalized icebreaker via OpenAI API, pings Slack `#sales-alerts`, and upserts to Google Sheets.\n   - **Tier 2 (Standard):** Logs directly to Google Sheets for batch nurturing.\n\n### Related Pre-Built Apify Tasks\n- [Substack Newsletter B2B Sponsorship Leads Scraper](https://apify.com/storeintel/substack-newsletter-b2b-sponsorship-leads-scraper)\n- [Substack Posts, Reactions & Engagement Scraper](https://apify.com/storeintel/substack-top-posts-engagement-metrics-scraper)\n- [Substack Paid Newsletter Authors & Socials Scraper](https://apify.com/storeintel/substack-paid-newsletter-authors-twitter-scraper)",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky-overview-8",
      "name": "Workflow Overview & Architecture",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        60,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Step 1: API Credentials Setup\n\n1. Sign in at [Apify Store — StoreIntel Labs](https://apify.com/storeintel/substack-newsletter-leads-posts-scraper) and copy your API token (`Settings -> Integrations`).\n2. In **2. Run StoreIntel Scraper**, select **Header Auth** (`Authorization: Bearer YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN`).\n3. Customize targets & `min_priority_score` (`70`) in **1. Configure Target Parameters**.\n4. Optional: Connect OpenAI **Bearer Auth** in node **7a** and **Slack OAuth2** in node **8a**.",
        "height": 290,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "sticky-setup-8",
      "name": "Step 1: Credentials & Targets",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        620,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Step 2: Lead Intent Scoring & AI Routing\n\n- **5. Compute Lead Intent Score (Code):** Inspects domain-specific high-intent signals (email reachability, pricing/MRR, churn rating, or enterprise tech stack) and calculates a 0–100 score.\n- **6. Route by Priority Tier (IF):** Records scoring **≥ 70** branch upward for instant LLM personalization + real-time Slack alert before saving to CRM.\n- Records below 70 bypass LLM costs and sync cleanly to Google Sheets.",
        "height": 290,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "sticky-scoring-8",
      "name": "Step 2: Intent Scoring & AI Routing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1140,
        60
      ]
    },
